{{ill|Kawanami Gokoku Shrine|ja|川南護国神社}} (川南護国神社{{ill|ja:川南護国神社|en}}) is a {{ill|Shinto shrine|en}} located in {{ill|Miyazaki Prefecture|Miyazaki Prefecture|en}}  {{ill|Japan|en}}. <!-- it is not a Beppyo shrine --> It is a {{ill|Gokoku Shrines|Gokoku Shrine|en}}, or a shrine dedicated to war dead.{{Efn|Is this {{ill|WP:BLUE|en}} considering that the shrine is literally named as such?}} Such shrines were made to serve to enshrine the war dead, and they were all considered "branches" of {{ill|Yasukuni Shrine|en}}. They were renamed from {{ill|Shōkonsha|Shokonsha|en}} in 1939.<ref>{{Cite journal|last=TAKAYAMA|first=K. PETER|date=1990|title=Enshrinement and Persistency of Japanese Religion|url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/23917081|journal=Journal of Church and State|volume=32|issue=3|pages=527–547|issn=0021-969X}}</ref><!-- derived from content I added to {{ill|Gokoku shrines|en}} from an english source -->It is the paratrooper shrine

